## Multiple Regression

Adding more predictors lets the model account for other sources of variation at the same time.


::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code}
library(gtsummary)

model <- lm(blood_pressure ~ age + treatment, data = data)
summary(model)
```

::: {.cell-output .cell-output-stdout}

```

Call:
lm(formula = blood_pressure ~ age + treatment, data = data)

Residuals:
    Min      1Q  Median      3Q     Max 
-36.380  -9.478  -2.054   9.323  35.338 

Coefficients:
            Estimate Std. Error t value Pr(>|t|)    
(Intercept) 105.8895     8.1296  13.025   <2e-16 ***
age           0.1702     0.1505   1.131    0.261    
treatmentB    6.5368     3.0219   2.163    0.033 *  
---
Signif. codes:  0 '***' 0.001 '**' 0.01 '*' 0.05 '.' 0.1 ' ' 1

Residual standard error: 14.95 on 97 degrees of freedom
Multiple R-squared:  0.05638,	Adjusted R-squared:  0.03693 
F-statistic: 2.898 on 2 and 97 DF,  p-value: 0.05992
```


:::

```{.r .cell-code}
# Using gtsummary for a publication-ready table
tbl_regression(model)
```

